<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26842" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">littĕrŭla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lītĕr-</span></b> ),
			ae, f.
		dim.
		littera. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little letter</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 6,
				9, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accepi tuam epistolam vacillantibus litterulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 16, 15, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: litterulae, ārum.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A short letter, a note</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc litterularum exaravi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 12, 1, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Grammatical knowledge, literary learning, liberal
				studies</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quem propter litterularum nescio quid libenter
					vidi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 7, 2, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterulae meae oblanguerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 16, 10, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 21, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterulis Graecis imbutus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
